IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-support`

-- ccc1-s8-20-general.l4 -- Part I (General), sections 8 to 20: application to the territories, the criminal law of England and the common law,
-- no common-law or imported offences, appeals for contempt of court, civil remedies, agreements and disclosure to the police, offences under more than one Act,
-- the child under twelve, consent to death, obedience to de facto law, mental disorder, compulsion, ignorance of the law, holidays.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: JUST TRUE = on the facts the provision gives the answer named; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (flat negative, "except", "if", "where",
-- "until"); NOTHING = not covered (a scope limit, a "who" description not met, a list not closed, silent). Bars are named as bars: JUST TRUE = barred. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A defence ("is exempt", "is excused") answers JUST FALSE as "this section gives no defence on these facts" where an "if" is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).

§ `Section 8 -- Application to territories, the criminal law of England, the common law`

-- src:535 | Application to territories
-- src:536 | 8 (1) The provisions of this Act apply throughout Canada except
-- src:537 | (a) in Yukon, in so far as they are inconsistent with the Yukon Act;
-- src:538 | (b) in the Northwest Territories, in so far as they are inconsistent with the Northwest Territories Act; and
-- src:539 | (c) in Nunavut, in so far as they are inconsistent with the Nunavut Act.
@ref s 8(1) (src:535-539)
GIVEN place IS A `Province or territory`
      `the provision is inconsistent, in so far as it applies in the place, with the Act that governs it (the Yukon Act, the Northwest Territories Act or the Nunavut Act)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) the provisions of this Act apply in the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN Yukon THEN
        IF `the provision is inconsistent, in so far as it applies in the place, with the Act that governs it (the Yukon Act, the Northwest Territories Act or the Nunavut Act)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except (a) in Yukon, in so far as they are inconsistent with the Yukon Act"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN
        IF `the provision is inconsistent, in so far as it applies in the place, with the Act that governs it (the Yukon Act, the Northwest Territories Act or the Nunavut Act)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the Northwest Territories, in so far as they are inconsistent with the Northwest Territories Act"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN Nunavut THEN
        IF `the provision is inconsistent, in so far as it applies in the place, with the Act that governs it (the Yukon Act, the Northwest Territories Act or the Nunavut Act)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in Nunavut, in so far as they are inconsistent with the Nunavut Act"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- every province: "The provisions of this Act apply throughout Canada"

-- src:540 | Application of criminal law of England
-- src:541 | (2) The criminal law of England that was in force in a province immediately before April 1, 1955 continues in force in the province except as altered, varied, modified or affected by this Act or any other Act of the Parliament of Canada.
@ref s 8(2) (src:540-541)
GIVEN `it is the criminal law of England that was in force in the province immediately before April 1, 1955` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is altered, varied, modified or affected by this Act or any other Act of the Parliament of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) the criminal law of England continues in force in the province` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is the criminal law of England that was in force in the province immediately before April 1, 1955` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The criminal law of England that was in force in a province immediately before April 1, 1955"
        IF `it is altered, varied, modified or affected by this Act or any other Act of the Parliament of Canada` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "continues in force in the province except as altered, varied, modified or affected by this Act or any other Act of the Parliament of Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:542 | Common law principles continued
-- src:543 | (3) Every rule and principle of the common law that renders any circumstance a justification or excuse for an act or a defence to a charge continues in force and applies in respect of proceedings for an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament except in so far as they are altered by or are inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament.
@ref s 8(3) (src:542-543)
GIVEN `the rule or principle of the common law renders a circumstance a justification or excuse for an act or a defence to a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is altered by or is inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the common law rule or principle continues in force and applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the rule or principle of the common law renders a circumstance a justification or excuse for an act or a defence to a charge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every rule and principle of the common law that renders any circumstance a justification or excuse for an act or a defence to a charge"
        IF NOT `the proceedings are for an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies in respect of proceedings for an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament"
        IF `it is altered by or is inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in so far as they are altered by or are inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 9 -- Criminal offences to be under law of Canada`

-- src:544 | Criminal offences to be under law of Canada
-- src:545 | 9 Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, no person shall be convicted or discharged under section 730
-- src:546 | (a) of an offence at common law,
-- src:547 | (b) of an offence under an Act of the Parliament of England, or of Great Britain, or of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, or
-- src:548 | (c) of an offence under an Act or ordinance in force in any province, territory or place before that province, territory or place became a province of Canada,
-- src:549 | but nothing in this section affects the power, jurisdiction or authority that a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge had, immediately before April 1, 1955, to impose punishment for contempt of court.
@ref s 9 (src:544-549)
DECLARE `s 9 the offence is` IS ONE OF
    `s 9(a) an offence at common law`
    `s 9(b) an offence under an Act of the Parliament of England, or of Great Britain, or of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland`
    `s 9(c) an offence under an Act or ordinance in force in any province, territory or place before that province, territory or place became a province of Canada`
    `s 9 an offence of none of those kinds`

@ref s 9 (src:544-549)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 9 the offence is`
      `it is the exercise of the power, jurisdiction or authority that a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge had, immediately before April 1, 1955, to impose punishment for contempt of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9 conviction or discharge under section 730 is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the exercise of the power, jurisdiction or authority that a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge had, immediately before April 1, 1955, to impose punishment for contempt of court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but nothing in this section affects the power, jurisdiction or authority that a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge had, immediately before April 1, 1955, to impose punishment for contempt of court"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 9 an offence of none of those kinds` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) of an offence at common law"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 10 -- Appeal for contempt of court`

-- src:550 | Appeal
-- src:551 | 10 (1) Where a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge summarily convicts a person for a contempt of court committed in the face of the court and imposes punishment in respect thereof, that person may appeal
-- src:552 | (a) from the conviction; or
-- src:553 | (b) against the punishment imposed.
@ref s 10(1) (src:550-553)
DECLARE `s 10 what is appealed` IS ONE OF
    `s 10(a) the conviction`
    `s 10(b) the punishment imposed`
    `s 10 something else`

@ref s 10(1) (src:550-553)
GIVEN `a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge summarily convicts the person for a contempt of court committed in the face of the court and imposes punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
      appeal IS A `s 10 what is appealed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) the person may appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge summarily convicts the person for a contempt of court committed in the face of the court and imposes punishment` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge summarily convicts a person for a contempt of court committed in the face of the court and imposes punishment in respect thereof"
        IF appeal EQUALS `s 10 something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "that person may appeal (a) from the conviction; or (b) against the punishment imposed" does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:554 | Idem
-- src:555 | (2) Where a court or judge summarily convicts a person for a contempt of court not committed in the face of the court and punishment is imposed in respect thereof, that person may appeal
-- src:556 | (a) from the conviction; or
-- src:557 | (b) against the punishment imposed.
@ref s 10(2) (src:554-557)
GIVEN `a court or judge summarily convicts the person for a contempt of court not committed in the face of the court and punishment is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      appeal IS A `s 10 what is appealed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) the person may appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court or judge summarily convicts the person for a contempt of court not committed in the face of the court and punishment is imposed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court or judge summarily convicts a person for a contempt of court not committed in the face of the court and punishment is imposed in respect thereof"
        IF appeal EQUALS `s 10 something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "that person may appeal (a) from the conviction; or (b) against the punishment imposed" does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:558 | Part XXI applies
-- src:559 | (3) An appeal under this section lies to the court of appeal of the province in which the proceedings take place, and, for the purposes of this section, the provisions of Part XXI apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref s 10(3) (src:558-559)
GIVEN `it is an appeal under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province or territory in which the proceedings take place` IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Province or territory`)
`s 10(3) the appeal lies to the court of appeal of the province in which the proceedings take place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an appeal under section 10` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal under this section lies to the court of appeal"
        IF `the place is a territory` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text says "the province in which the proceedings take place" and does not say what lies for a territory
        OTHERWISE JUST `the province or territory in which the proceedings take place`
    WHERE
        `the place is a territory` MEANS
            `the province or territory in which the proceedings take place` EQUALS Yukon
            OR `the province or territory in which the proceedings take place` EQUALS `Northwest Territories`
            OR `the province or territory in which the proceedings take place` EQUALS Nunavut

@ref s 10(3) (src:559-559)
GIVEN `it is an appeal under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3) the provisions of Part XXI apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF `it is an appeal under section 10`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of this section, the provisions of Part XXI apply"

§ `Sections 11 and 11.1 -- Civil remedy; non-disclosure agreement`

-- src:560 | Civil remedy not suspended
-- src:561 | 11 No civil remedy for an act or omission is suspended or affected by reason that the act or omission is a criminal offence.
@ref s 11 (src:560-561)
GIVEN `the act or omission is a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11 a civil remedy is suspended or affected by reason that the act or omission is a criminal offence` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission is a criminal offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No civil remedy for an act or omission is suspended or affected by reason that the act or omission is a criminal offence."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 11 speaks only of the fact that the act or omission is a criminal offence

-- src:562 | Non-disclosure agreement — no effect
-- src:563 | 11.1 For greater certainty, no agreement may prevent or restrict a person from disclosing any information that relates to the commission of an offence to a police officer.
@ref s 11.1 (src:562-563)
GIVEN `the information relates to the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11.1 an agreement may prevent or restrict the person from disclosing the information` MEANS
    IF `the information relates to the commission of an offence` AND `the disclosure is to a police officer`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no agreement may prevent or restrict a person from disclosing any information that relates to the commission of an offence to a police officer"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information that relates to the commission of an offence to a police officer"

§ `Section 12 -- Offence punishable under more than one Act`

-- src:564 | Offence punishable under more than one Act
-- src:565 | 12 Where an act or omission is an offence under more than one Act of Parliament, whether punishable by indictment or on summary conviction, a person who does the act or makes the omission is, unless a contrary intention appears, subject to proceedings under any of those Acts, but is not liable to be punished more than once for the same offence.
@ref s 12 (src:564-565)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence under more than one Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 the person is subject to proceedings under any of those Acts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is an offence under more than one Act of Parliament` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an act or omission is an offence under more than one Act of Parliament"
        IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless a contrary intention appears"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 12 (src:565-565)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence under more than one Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has already been punished for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 the person is liable to be punished again for the same offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is an offence under more than one Act of Parliament` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an act or omission is an offence under more than one Act of Parliament"
        IF `the person has already been punished for the same offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not liable to be punished more than once for the same offence"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 12 says nothing of a person not yet punished once

§ `Sections 13 to 15 -- Child under twelve, consent to death, obedience to de facto law`

-- src:566 | Child under twelve
-- src:567 | 13 No person shall be convicted of an offence in respect of an act or omission on his part while that person was under the age of twelve years.
@ref s 13 (src:566-567)
GIVEN `the age in years of the person at the time of the act or omission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 conviction is barred because the person was under the age of twelve years at the time of the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the age in years of the person at the time of the act or omission` LESS THAN 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "while that person was under the age of twelve years"

-- src:568 | Consent to death
-- src:569 | 14 No person is entitled to consent to have death inflicted on them, and such consent does not affect the criminal responsibility of any person who inflicts death on the person who gave consent.
@ref s 14 (src:568-569)
GIVEN `the consent is to have death inflicted on the person who gives it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14 a person is entitled to consent to have death inflicted on them` MEANS
    IF `the consent is to have death inflicted on the person who gives it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person is entitled to consent to have death inflicted on them"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 14 speaks only of consent to have death inflicted

@ref s 14 (src:569-569)
GIVEN `death is inflicted on the person who gave consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14 the consent affects the criminal responsibility of the person who inflicts death` MEANS
    IF `death is inflicted on the person who gave consent`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such consent does not affect the criminal responsibility of any person who inflicts death on the person who gave consent"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who inflicts death on the person who gave consent"

-- src:570 | Obedience to de facto law
-- src:571 | 15 No person shall be convicted of an offence in respect of an act or omission in obedience to the laws for the time being made and enforced by persons in de facto possession of the sovereign power in and over the place where the act or omission occurs.
@ref s 15 (src:570-571)
GIVEN `the act or omission was in obedience to the laws for the time being made and enforced by persons in de facto possession of the sovereign power in and over the place where the act or omission occurs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 conviction is barred because the act or omission was in obedience to the laws made and enforced by persons in de facto possession of the sovereign power` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission was in obedience to the laws for the time being made and enforced by persons in de facto possession of the sovereign power in and over the place where the act or omission occurs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in obedience to the laws for the time being made and enforced by persons in de facto possession of the sovereign power in and over the place where the act or omission occurs"

§ `Section 16 -- Defence of mental disorder`

-- src:572 | Defence of mental disorder
-- src:573 | 16 (1) No person is criminally responsible for an act committed or an omission made while suffering from a mental disorder that rendered the person incapable of appreciating the nature and quality of the act or omission or of knowing that it was wrong.
@ref s 16(1) (src:572-573)
GIVEN `s 2 mental disorder: the person was suffering from one when the act was committed or the omission made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it rendered the person incapable of appreciating the nature and quality of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it rendered the person incapable of knowing that it was wrong` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the person is exempt from criminal responsibility` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 mental disorder: the person was suffering from one when the act was committed or the omission made` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person suffered from a mental disorder is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `s 2 mental disorder: the person was suffering from one when the act was committed or the omission made` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "while suffering from a mental disorder"
        IF `it rendered the person incapable of appreciating the nature and quality of the act or omission` OR `it rendered the person incapable of knowing that it was wrong` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that rendered the person incapable of appreciating the nature and quality of the act or omission or of knowing that it was wrong"

-- src:574 | Presumption
-- src:575 | (2) Every person is presumed not to suffer from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection (1), until the contrary is proved on the balance of probabilities.
@ref s 16(2) (src:574-575)
GIVEN `the contrary has been proved on the balance of probabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2) the person is presumed not to suffer from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility` MEANS
    IF `the contrary has been proved on the balance of probabilities`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the contrary is proved on the balance of probabilities"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:576 | Burden of proof
-- src:577 | (3) The burden of proof that an accused was suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility is on the party that raises the issue.
@ref s 16(3) (src:576-577)
GIVEN `the issue is raised that the accused was suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party that raises the issue` IS A Party
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`s 16(3) the burden of proof is on the party that raises the issue` MEANS
    IF `the issue is raised that the accused was suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility`
    THEN JUST `the party that raises the issue`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is on the party that raises the issue"

§ `Sections 17 to 19 -- Compulsion by threats, compulsion of spouse, ignorance of the law`

-- src:578 | Compulsion by threats
-- src:579 | 17 A person who commits an offence under compulsion by threats of immediate death or bodily harm from a person who is present when the offence is committed is excused for committing the offence if the person believes that the threats will be carried out and if the person is not a party to a conspiracy or association whereby the person is subject to compulsion, but this section does not apply where the offence that is committed is high treason or treason, murder, piracy, attempted murder, sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm, aggravated sexual assault, forcible abduction, hostage taking, robbery, assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm, aggravated assault, unlawfully causing bodily harm, arson or an offence under sections 280 to 283 (abduction and detention of young persons).
@ref s 17 (src:578-579)
DECLARE `s 17 the offence committed` IS ONE OF
    `s 17 high treason`
    `s 17 treason`
    `s 17 murder`
    `s 17 piracy`
    `s 17 attempted murder`
    `s 17 sexual assault`
    `s 17 sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm`
    `s 17 aggravated sexual assault`
    `s 17 forcible abduction`
    `s 17 hostage taking`
    `s 17 robbery`
    `s 17 assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm`
    `s 17 aggravated assault`
    `s 17 unlawfully causing bodily harm`
    `s 17 arson`
    `s 17 an offence under sections 280 to 283 (abduction and detention of young persons)`
    `s 17 an offence not in that list`

@ref s 17 (src:578-579)
GIVEN `the person commits the offence under compulsion by threats from a person who is present when the offence is committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the threat is of immediate death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 bodily harm: the threat is of immediate bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person believes that the threats will be carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to a conspiracy or association whereby the person is subject to compulsion` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `s 17 the offence committed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 the section excuses the person for committing the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person commits the offence under compulsion by threats from a person who is present when the offence is committed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who commits an offence under compulsion by threats of immediate death or bodily harm from a person who is present when the offence is committed"
        IF `the threat` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the harm threatened is bodily harm is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `the threat` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "threats of immediate death or bodily harm"
        IF NOT (offence EQUALS `s 17 an offence not in that list`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but this section does not apply where the offence that is committed is high treason or treason, murder, piracy, attempted murder, sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm, aggravated sexual assault, forcible abduction, hostage taking, robbery, assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm, aggravated assault, unlawfully causing bodily harm, arson or an offence under sections 280 to 283"
        IF NOT `the person believes that the threats will be carried out` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is excused for committing the offence if the person believes that the threats will be carried out"
        IF `the person is a party to a conspiracy or association whereby the person is subject to compulsion` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if the person is not a party to a conspiracy or association whereby the person is subject to compulsion"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the threat` MEANS `ccc1 either of` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the threat is of immediate death`) `s 2 bodily harm: the threat is of immediate bodily harm`

-- src:580 | Compulsion of spouse
-- src:581 | 18 No presumption arises that a married person who commits an offence does so under compulsion by reason only that the offence is committed in the presence of the spouse of that married person.
@ref s 18 (src:580-581)
GIVEN `the person is a married person who commits an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed in the presence of the person's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only reason for supposing that the person acted under compulsion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18 a presumption arises that the married person acted under compulsion` MEANS
    IF `the person is a married person who commits an offence` AND `the offence is committed in the presence of the person's spouse` AND `that is the only reason for supposing that the person acted under compulsion`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No presumption arises that a married person who commits an offence does so under compulsion by reason only that the offence is committed in the presence of the spouse of that married person."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that the offence is committed in the presence of the spouse"

-- src:582 | Ignorance of the law
-- src:583 | 19 Ignorance of the law by a person who commits an offence is not an excuse for committing that offence.
@ref s 19 (src:582-583)
GIVEN `the person committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's ignorance is of the law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 ignorance of the law is an excuse for committing the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person committed an offence` AND `the person's ignorance is of the law`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Ignorance of the law by a person who commits an offence is not an excuse for committing that offence."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Ignorance of the law by a person who commits an offence"

§ `Section 20 -- Certain acts on holidays valid`

-- src:584 | Certain acts on holidays valid
-- src:585 | 20 A warrant, summons, appearance notice, undertaking, release order or recognizance that is authorized by this Act may be executed, issued, given or entered into, as the case may be, on a holiday.
@ref s 20 (src:584-585)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `it is authorized by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day is a holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20 the document may be executed, issued, given or entered into on a holiday` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the document is one the section names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names a warrant, summons, appearance notice, undertaking, release order or recognizance and says nothing of the other documents
        IF NOT `it is authorized by this Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is authorized by this Act"
        IF NOT `the day is a holiday` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on a holiday"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the document is one the section names` MEANS
            document EQUALS `a warrant for arrest` OR document EQUALS `a search warrant` OR document EQUALS `a summons` OR document EQUALS `an appearance notice`
            OR document EQUALS `an undertaking` OR document EQUALS `a release order` OR document EQUALS `a recognizance`
